\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Hark! the herald-angels sing
\par Glory to the new-born King,
\par Peace on earth, and mercy mild,
\par God and sinners reconciled,
\par Joyful, all ye nations, rise,
\par Join the triumph of the skies;
\par With the angelic host proclaim,
\par Christ is born in Bethlehem.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Hark! the herald-angels sing
\par Glory to the new-born King.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Christ, by highest heaven adored,
\par Christ, the everlasting Lord,
\par Late in time behold Him come,
\par Offspring of a virgin's womb!
\par Veiled in flesh the Godhead see;
\par Hail the incarnate Deity!
\par Pleased as man with men to dwell,
\par Jesus, our Immanuel.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Hark! the herald-angels sing
\par Glory to the new-born King.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Mild He lays His glory by,
\par Born that man no more may die,
\par Born to raise the sons of earth,
\par Born to give them second birth.
\par Hail the heaven-born Prince of Peace!
\par Hail the Sun of Righteousness!
\par Light and Life to all He brings,
\par Risen with healing in His wings.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Hark! the herald-angels sing
\par Glory to the new-born King.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

